# Community Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We pledge to make participation in this project welcoming and respectful to everyone, regardless of background, identity, experience, or personal characteristics. We will act in ways that support an open, inclusive, and constructive community.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include listening with care, respecting differing viewpoints, giving and accepting constructive feedback, and taking responsibility for mistakes. Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, insults, discriminatory language, unwanted advances, publishing private information without consent, and conduct that would be inappropriate in a professional setting.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying these standards and responding fairly to reports. They may remove, edit, or reject contributions that violate this Code and will explain moderation decisions when appropriate.

## Scope

This Code applies in project spaces, including the repository, issue tracker, and pull requests. It also applies when someone represents the project in public or online spaces.

## Enforcement

Report abusive or harmful behavior privately to the project maintainers through the repository's contact method. Maintainers will review reports promptly, respect the reporter's privacy, and take appropriate action.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Maintainers will consider the impact, severity, and context of each incident. They may issue a private correction, a formal warning, a temporary restriction from project spaces, or a permanent ban for repeated or severe violations. People asked to stop harmful behavior are expected to comply immediately.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is informed by the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1: https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct/ .
